module

public import TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.Homotopy.Hurewicz.Spherical
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.Singular.MinimalGenus
public import TauCeti.Geometry.Manifold.Complex.FundamentalClass
public import TauCeti.Geometry.Symplectic.Manifold.PrestableMap

/-!
# The homology class of a prestable map

A prestable map from a nodal curve to a space `X` (`TauCeti.IsPrestableMap`) is a family of maps
on the normalization components `C i` of the curve, compact Riemann surfaces, which agree at the
two points of every node. Its **class** is the sum of the images of the fundamental classes of the
components,

`∑ i, (u ∘ ι_i)_*[C i] ∈ H₂(X; ℤ)`,

where `ι_i : C i → Σ i, C i` is the inclusion of a component and `[C i]` is the fundamental class
of the complex orientation (`TauCeti.complexFundamentalClass`). The moduli spaces of stable maps
are split by this class, and the class enters the energy of a pseudoholomorphic stable map, its
index and the Novikov variable that weights it.

The class only uses the continuity of the map on the normalization, so it is defined for every
continuous map `u : Σ i, C i → X` (`TauCeti.normalizationClass`); the class of a prestable map
`u` is `normalizationClass ⟨u, hu.continuous⟩`. The normalization `Σ i, C i` of a curve with
finitely many components is itself a compact Riemann surface, disconnected in general, and its
fundamental class is the sum of those of its components (`TauCeti.complexFundamentalClass_sigma`).
So the class is also the image `u_*[Σ i, C i]` of the fundamental class of the normalization,
which is how it is defined here, and the sum formula is
`TauCeti.normalizationClass_eq_sum`.

* **Invariance under isomorphisms.** A biholomorphism of normalizations
  `Φ : Σ i, C i ≃ Σ j, C' j`, such as the underlying map of an isomorphism of nodal curves
  `TauCeti.NodalGluing.Iso`, possibly permuting the components, carries fundamental class to
  fundamental class. Hence `u' ∘ Φ` and `u'` have the same class
  (`TauCeti.normalizationClass_comp_diffeomorph`): prestable maps related by an isomorphism of
  their nodal curves have the same class.
* **Naturality.** Composing with a continuous map `g : X → Y` maps the class by `g_*`
  (`TauCeti.singularHomologyFunctor_map_normalizationClass`).
* **Constant maps.** A constant map has class `0`, since it factors through a point
  (`TauCeti.normalizationClass_const`).
* **Genus zero.** If every component is simply connected, as is a compact Riemann surface of
  genus zero, then the class is spherical: its image in `H₂(X; ℤ)` with integer coefficients lies
  in the subgroup `TauCeti.sphericalClasses X 1` generated by the Hurewicz images of maps of
  spheres (`TauCeti.map_uliftIntIso_normalizationClass_mem_sphericalClasses`). Indeed every
  class of `H₂(C i; ℤ)` of a simply connected `C i` is spherical, and spherical classes are
  natural. This is the topological reason why genus-zero stable maps, and the genus-zero
  invariants counting them, only meet the spherical classes of `X`, over which the period group of
  capped Hamiltonian Floer theory is formed.

The descent of a prestable map to the compact nodal quotient
(`TauCeti.IsPrestableMap.continuous_lift`) and the comparison of the class with the image of a
fundamental class of that quotient are not treated here.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.normalizationClass`: the class `u_*[Σ i, C i] = ∑ i, (u ∘ ι_i)_*[C i]` of a continuous
  map from the normalization of a nodal curve.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.normalizationClass_eq_sum`: the class is the sum of the images of the fundamental
  classes of the components.
* `TauCeti.normalizationClass_comp_diffeomorph`: the class is invariant under biholomorphisms of
  the normalization.
* `TauCeti.singularHomologyFunctor_map_normalizationClass`: naturality in the target.
* `TauCeti.normalizationClass_const`: constant maps have class `0`.
* `TauCeti.map_uliftIntIso_normalizationClass_mem_sphericalClasses`: maps from curves with
  simply connected components have spherical classes.

## References

* D. McDuff and D. Salamon, *J-holomorphic Curves and Symplectic Topology*, 2nd ed., AMS Colloquium
  Publications 52 (2012), §5.1, for stable maps on nodal curves and their classes.
* A. Hatcher, [*Algebraic Topology*](https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf),
  Section 4.2, for the Hurewicz map and spherical classes.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Topology AlgebraicTopology
open scoped Manifold ContDiff

namespace TauCeti

variable {ι : Type} {C : ι → Type} [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (C i)] [∀ i, T2Space (C i)]
  [∀ i, ChartedSpace ℂ (C i)] [∀ i, IsManifold 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) 1 (C i)] [Finite ι]
  [∀ i, CompactSpace (C i)] {X Y : Type} [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Y]

/-- The **homology class** `u_*[Σ i, C i] ∈ H₂(X; ℤ)` of a continuous map `u` from the
normalization `Σ i, C i` of a nodal curve, with finitely many compact Riemann surfaces `C i` as
components: the image of the fundamental class of the normalization for its complex orientation.
It is the sum `∑ i, (u ∘ ι_i)_*[C i]` of the images of the fundamental classes of the components
(`TauCeti.normalizationClass_eq_sum`). The class of a prestable map `u`
(`TauCeti.IsPrestableMap`) is `normalizationClass ⟨u, hu.continuous⟩`. -/
def normalizationClass (u : C((Σ i, C i), X)) : secondHomology X :=
  (complexHomologicalOrientation (Σ i, C i)).mapFundamentalClass Complex.finrank_real_complex u

theorem normalizationClass_def (u : C((Σ i, C i), X)) :
    normalizationClass u =
      (complexHomologicalOrientation (Σ i, C i)).mapFundamentalClass Complex.finrank_real_complex
        u :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The class of a map from a nodal curve is the sum of the classes of its components**: the
sum of the images `(u ∘ ι_i)_*[C i]` of the fundamental classes of the components. -/
theorem normalizationClass_eq_sum [Fintype ι] (u : C((Σ i, C i), X)) :
    normalizationClass u =
      ∑ i, (complexHomologicalOrientation (C i)).mapFundamentalClass Complex.finrank_real_complex
        (u.comp ⟨Sigma.mk i, continuous_sigmaMk⟩) := by
  rw [normalizationClass_def, HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass_def,
    ← complexFundamentalClass_def, complexFundamentalClass_sigma, map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
  rw [HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass_comp]

/-- **Invariance under biholomorphisms of the normalization.** For a `C^k` biholomorphism
`Φ : Σ i, C i ≃ Σ j, C' j`, `k ≠ 0`, such as the underlying map of an isomorphism of nodal curves
(`TauCeti.NodalGluing.Iso`), the maps `u ∘ Φ` and `u` have the same class. In particular two
prestable maps related by an isomorphism of their nodal curves have the same class. -/
@[simp]
theorem normalizationClass_comp_diffeomorph {ι' : Type} {C' : ι' → Type}
    [∀ j, TopologicalSpace (C' j)] [∀ j, T2Space (C' j)] [∀ j, ChartedSpace ℂ (C' j)]
    [∀ j, IsManifold 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) 1 (C' j)] [Finite ι'] [∀ j, CompactSpace (C' j)] {k : ℕ∞ω}
    [NeZero k] (Φ : (Σ i, C i) ≃ₘ^k⟮𝓘(ℂ, ℂ), 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ)⟯ Σ j, C' j) (u : C((Σ j, C' j), X)) :
    normalizationClass (u.comp (Φ.toHomeomorph : C((Σ i, C i), Σ j, C' j))) =
      normalizationClass u :=
  Φ.mapFundamentalClass_complexHomologicalOrientation_comp u

/-- **Naturality of the class in the target.** The map `g_* : H₂(X; ℤ) → H₂(Y; ℤ)` induced by a
continuous map `g : X → Y` sends the class of `u` to the class of `g ∘ u`. -/
@[simp]
theorem singularHomologyFunctor_map_normalizationClass (g : C(X, Y)) (u : C((Σ i, C i), X)) :
    (((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) 2).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))).map
      (TopCat.ofHom g)).hom (normalizationClass u) = normalizationClass (g.comp u) := by
  rw [normalizationClass_def, normalizationClass_def,
    HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass_comp]

/-- **Constant maps have class zero**: a constant map factors through a point, whose second
homology vanishes. -/
@[simp]
theorem normalizationClass_const (x : X) :
    normalizationClass (ContinuousMap.const (Σ i, C i) x) = 0 := by
  rw [normalizationClass_def, HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass_def,
    singularHomologyFunctor_map_const_eq_zero _ x two_ne_zero]
  exact LinearMap.zero_apply _

/-- **Maps from curves with simply connected components have spherical classes.** If every
component `C i` is simply connected, as a compact Riemann surface of genus zero is, then the class
of every continuous map from the normalization, read with integer coefficients, is spherical: it
lies in the subgroup of `H₂(X; ℤ)` generated by the Hurewicz images of maps of spheres. In
particular the class of a genus-zero prestable map is spherical. -/
theorem map_uliftIntIso_normalizationClass_mem_sphericalClasses
    [∀ i, SimplyConnectedSpace (C i)] (u : C((Σ i, C i), X)) :
    (((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) 2).map uliftIntIso.hom).app (TopCat.of X)).hom
      (normalizationClass u) ∈ sphericalClasses X 1 := by
  cases nonempty_fintype ι
  rw [normalizationClass_eq_sum, map_sum]
  refine AddSubgroup.sum_mem _ fun i _ ↦ ?_
  -- Changing coefficients from `ULift ℤ` to `ℤ` commutes with pushing forward along `u ∘ ι_i`.
  have hnat := congrArg (fun φ ↦ φ.hom (complexFundamentalClass (C i)))
    (((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) 2).map uliftIntIso.hom).naturality
      (TopCat.ofHom (u.comp ⟨Sigma.mk i, continuous_sigmaMk⟩)))
  simp only [ModuleCat.hom_comp] at hnat
  rw [HomologicalOrientation.mapFundamentalClass_def, ← complexFundamentalClass_def]
  refine hnat ▸ map_mem_sphericalClasses (u.comp ⟨Sigma.mk i, continuous_sigmaMk⟩) ?_
  rw [sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace]
  exact AddSubgroup.mem_top _

end TauCeti
